### Problem 2: Concurrency & Race Conditions

**Issue**: Multiple requests writing simultaneously.

**Solution Implemented**:
```javascript
// All operations save immediately
create(post) {
  // ... add to map
  this.save(); // Atomic file write
}

update(id, updates) {
  // ... modify
  this.save(); // Atomic file write
}
```

**Production**: Use transactions
```javascript
// PostgreSQL with transactions
async function updatePostWithFeedback(id, updates) {
  const client = await pool.connect();
  try {
    await client.query('BEGIN');
    await client.query('UPDATE blogs SET ... WHERE id = $1', [id]);
    await client.query('INSERT INTO blog_feedback ... VALUES (...)');
    await client.query('COMMIT');
  } catch (err) {
    await client.query('ROLLBACK');
    throw err;
  } finally {
    client.release();
  }
}
```

